WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.333 --> 00:00:02.302
-So this show is based on
"Glorious Ladies of Wrestling,"

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:03.069 size:84% position:42% line:92%
which was a real thing.

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:05.405
-Seth, it's
"Gorgeous Ladies of Wrestling."

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:07.073 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-Gorgeous, I apologize.

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:08.141 line:92%
I'm so ashamed of myself.

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:09.876
-You said the same thing
when my husband was here.

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:11.911
And I just want you to know.
-Oh, I got it wrong then too?

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:13.546 align:start size:94% position:6%
Oh, my God.
-That it's "gorgeous."

00:00:13.546 --> 00:00:15.882 size:81% position:41%
-Well, first of all,
I guess the difference

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:17.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
between the two of you
as a couple,

00:00:17.217 --> 00:00:18.918 line:92%
is that he didn't correct me.

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:21.621 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:27.560
-They call -- They refer to him
as the polite one in the couple.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:30.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, I was so excited,
but well, here's the thing,

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:31.097 size:78% position:39% line:92%
'cause I was aware --

00:00:31.097 --> 00:00:32.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's even more embarrassing
for me,

00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:34.501
because I was aware of "Gorgeous
Ladies of Wrestling."

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:35.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
I remember watching it.
-You watched it?

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:40.840
-Yeah, because I was at the age
where it was almost sexual,

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:42.675
but I couldn't quite figure out
why.

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:43.376 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Sure. Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:45.812 size:81% position:41%
That's still sort of
what our show is like.

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:46.246 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:49.482 align:start size:94% position:6%
But were you -- Did you have
any familiarity with --

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:51.918 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-None, no, none at all.

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:53.119 line:92%
My agents called me to say

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:55.255
Jenji Kohan is producing a show
for Netflix.

00:00:55.255 --> 00:00:57.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's about a women's wrestling
show from the '80s.

00:00:57.957 --> 00:00:59.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was kind of like,
"What an idea!"

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:01.361
And they were like, "No, it was
a real thing."

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:05.899
And I started googling it,
and the videos are crazy.

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:07.534 line:92%
It's the most bizarre thing

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:08.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it wasn't
just wrestling.

00:01:08.535 --> 00:01:12.072
It was like a real outlier from
what wrestling was at the '80s.

00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:14.441
And it's like Hulk Hogan and the
Iron Sheik and stuff like that.

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:18.111 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then these are like, women
of all shapes and sizes.

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:18.711 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Like on our show,

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:21.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
they were actresses and models
who got cast on this show

00:01:21.281 --> 00:01:22.482 line:92%
and learned how to wrestle.

00:01:22.482 --> 00:01:24.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
They don't just wrestle
on the show.

00:01:24.117 --> 00:01:26.119 line:92%
They do sketches and they rap.

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:28.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-They -- They "rap."

00:01:28.822 --> 00:01:30.757 line:92%
-Yeah. There was a weird --

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:33.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
Post the Chicago Bears
Super Bowl Shuffle,

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:35.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
there was a weird, low bar
for rap.

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:38.298 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure, Blondie rapped in
"Rapture."

00:01:38.298 --> 00:01:39.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel like that's what their
style of rapping --

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:43.002
-Is it true that you had to rap
for the audition?

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:46.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, so, yes and no.
-Okay.

00:01:46.306 --> 00:01:49.576
-They -- As part of the
audition, they included a vid--

00:01:49.576 --> 00:01:53.046
They said, "You're going to come
in and do something like this,"

00:01:53.046 --> 00:01:54.747 line:92%
and included a video of the rap

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:57.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then had sample, I guess,
rap lyrics

00:01:57.650 --> 00:01:59.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
and also told us
we could improvise.

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:01.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
And later, after we all
got on the show,

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:03.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
the women were all
telling their stories --

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:03.857 line:92%
the other girls on the show --

00:02:03.857 --> 00:02:05.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
about what they rapped
in their audition.

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:07.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like, "Oh, everyone
just rapped that?"

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:11.731
I'm so my character Ruth
on the show that I read it

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:13.366
and was like, "I'm not going to
rap that,

00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:16.269
'cause it would be better as
a monologue. I will monologue.

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:20.306
I'm gonna monologue that,"
and went in and improvised.

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:22.375
But I still think that
the reason I got the job,

00:02:22.375 --> 00:02:25.245 align:start size:94% position:6%
we improvised
in our wrestling character.

00:02:25.245 --> 00:02:28.781
So I was being this, like,
Russian villainous character.

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:33.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think I got the job
because of my improv about --

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:36.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
I basically was rhyming
Natasha and Boris.

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:38.024 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's a good Russian
reference.

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:41.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
-With, you know,
"stomp on your clitoris."

00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:42.362 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, there you go.

00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:42.896 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.896 --> 00:02:45.932
It turns out, you know what, you
picked something up in Compton.

00:02:45.932 --> 00:02:47.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
You picked something up
in Compton.

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:48.701 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It came around.

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:51.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And by the way,
I would be remiss to not show,

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:53.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
you got in
incredibly good shape.

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:58.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah.
-There you are, wrestling.

00:02:58.077 --> 00:03:01.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, yeah, when Dave was here,
he was saying that --

00:03:01.881 --> 00:03:04.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was this -- I mean,
have you ever had a part

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:05.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
where you had to get in shape
like this ever?

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:07.754 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No. I've been dying to have
a part like this.

00:03:07.754 --> 00:03:09.088
And I've trained with my trainer
for a long time

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:11.824
and was really excited to do it,
but I would never imagine

00:03:11.824 --> 00:03:13.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I would do anything
like wrestling.

00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:17.530
So it was very cool to, like, be
getting stronger and doing,

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:19.866 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, extra strength training
and then also,

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:21.201 line:92%
to be learning how to wrestle

00:03:21.201 --> 00:03:23.703
and use our body in that way was
very empowering and cool.

00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:25.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's great.
And the show is really great.

00:03:25.672 --> 00:03:28.274
And congratulations, and it's
always so nice to see you.

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:29.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much
for being Alison.

00:03:29.676 --> 00:03:31.411 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Alison Brie, everybody!

